      "code": "if (irep && pc < irep->ilen) {\n  if (!irep->debug_info) {\n    *lp = -1; *fp = NULL;\n    return FALSE;\n  }\n  mrb_irep_debug_info_file *f = get_file(irep->debug_info, pc);\n  *lp = debug_get_line(mrb, f, pc);\n  if (*lp > 0) {\n    *fp = debug_get_filename(mrb, f);\n    if (*fp) return TRUE;\n  }\n}\nreturn FALSE;",
      "note": "On the crashing path `each_backtrace()` passes `&loc.lineno` and `&loc.filename`. Because step 10's `idx` is outside `irep->ilen`, the function returns `FALSE` with both outputs untouched, so the uninitialized contents of step 8's stack local remain live. The staged patch adds `*lp = -1; *fp = NULL;` before the final return to satisfy that missing initialization obligation.",
